  MF2:  Resolved resonance range  (RRR)                           3925 1451   32
       The RRR was generated with TARES-1.2, compiled on          3925 1451   33
       02-28-2014 10:42:45 AM at Petten, the, Netherlands. The RRR3925 1451   34
       expands from 0 to 2.781615E+5 eV, with resonance           3925 1451   35
       extracted from the "radiator" TARES database. A total of   3925 1451   36
       3 l-values are used and 335 resonances. The resonance      3925 1451   37
       formalism is multi-level Breit Wigner (MLBW).              3925 1451   38
       The ladder approach from the CALENDF code is used to       3925 1451   39
       generate statistical resonances in the unresolved          3925 1451   40
       resonance range. Therefore, the URR is translated into     3925 1451   41
       resolved resonance range. Explanations about the method    3925 1451   42
       can be found in the CALENDF manual: CEA-Report CEA-R-6277  3925 1451   43
       "CALENDF-2010: User manual" by J.C. Sublet, P. Ribon and   3925 1451   44
       M. Coste-Delcaux.                                          3925 1451   45
       The method of creating statistical resonances in the       3925 1451   46
       URR region is described in: "From average parameters to    3925 1451   47
       statistical resolved resonances", D. Rochman et al.,       3925 1451   48
       Annals of Nucl. Ene. 51 (2013) 60.                         3925 1451   49
       The s-wave average level spacing is 3699 eV and            3925 1451   50
       the s-wave neutron strength is 4.653e-05 1e-4.             3925 1451   51
